var practiceQs=[{id:43241,text:"📏 The p-adic absolute value satisfies which inequality?",opts:[{l:"A",t:"|x+y|_p ≤ max(|x|_p, |y|_p)",c:true},{l:"B",t:"|x+y|_p ≤ |x|_p + |y|_p",c:false},{l:"C",t:"|x+y|_p = |x|_p + |y|_p",c:false},{l:"D",t:"|x+y|_p ≥ |x|_p + |y|_p",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>ultrametric triangle inequality</strong>: |x+y|_p ≤ max(|x|_p, |y|_p) — this is stronger than the usual triangle inequality and makes ℚ_p an ultrametric space."},{id:43242,text:"📏 The ring of p-adic integers ℤ_p can be described as:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"The inverse limit lim← ℤ/pⁿℤ",c:true},{l:"B",t:"The direct limit lim→ ℤ/pⁿℤ",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The field of fractions of ℤ",c:false},{l:"D",t:"The algebraic closure of ℚ_p",c:false}],sol:"<strong>ℤ_p = lim← ℤ/pⁿℤ</strong> is the inverse limit of the finite rings ℤ/pⁿℤ under the natural reduction maps — equivalently, the set of sequences (a_n) with a_n ∈ ℤ/pⁿℤ compatible mod pⁿ."},{id:43243,text:"📏 Hensel's lemma requires which condition to lift a root mod p to ℤ_p?",opts:[{l:"A",t:"f(a) ≡ 0 mod p and f'(a) not ≡ 0 mod p",c:true},{l:"B",t:"f(a) ≡ 0 mod p²",c:false},{l:"C",t:"f'(a) ≡ 0 mod p",c:false},{l:"D",t:"f is constant",c:false}],sol:"<strong>Hensel's lemma</strong>: if f ∈ ℤ_p[x], f(a) ≡ 0 (mod p), and f'(a) ≢ 0 (mod p), then there exists a unique b ∈ ℤ_p with f(b)=0 and b ≡ a (mod p). The non-vanishing of the derivative modulo p ensures a simple root."},{id:43244,text:"🌍 A function f: ℤ_p → ℚ_p has a Mahler expansion f(x) = Σ a_n (x choose n). The coefficients a_n are given by:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"The nth finite difference (Δⁿ f)(0)",c:true},{l:"B",t:"The nth derivative f^{(n)}(0)/n!",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The integral of f over ℤ_p",c:false},{l:"D",t:"The Fourier coefficients of f",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Mahler coefficients</strong> a_n = (Δⁿ f)(0), where Δ is the forward difference operator (Δf)(x) = f(x+1) − f(x). This is the p-adic analogue of Taylor coefficients."},{id:43245,text:"🌍 For convergence of a power series Σ a_n xⁿ on all of ℤ_p, what condition on |a_n|_p is necessary?",opts:[{l:"A",t:"|a_n|_p → 0 as n → ∞",c:true},{l:"B",t:"|a_n|_p → ∞ as n → ∞",c:false},{l:"C",t:"|a_n|_p = 1 for all n",c:false},{l:"D",t:"|a_n|_p is constant",c:false}],sol:"For an <strong>analytic function</strong> on ℤ_p, we need |a_n|_p → 0 as n → ∞ so that the power series converges for all x ∈ ℤ_p (since |xⁿ|_p ≤ 1)."},{id:43246,text:"🌍 The p-adic Fourier transform of a measure μ on ℤ_p is defined as:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"̂μ(χ) = ∫ χ(x) dμ(x)",c:true},{l:"B",t:"̂μ(χ) = ∫ xⁿ dμ(x)",c:false},{l:"C",t:"̂μ(χ) = Σ μ({x})·χ(x)",c:false},{l:"D",t:"̂μ(χ) = ∫ e^{2πix} dμ(x)",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>p-adic Fourier transform</strong> ̂μ(χ) = ∫ χ(x) dμ(x) for characters χ: ℤ_p → ℂ_p^×, paralleling classical Fourier analysis but with p-adic-valued characters."},{id:43247,text:"🧮 Morita's p-adic gamma function Γ_p satisfies which functional equation for x ∈ ℤ_p^×?",opts:[{l:"A",t:"Γ_p(x+1) = −x·Γ_p(x)",c:true},{l:"B",t:"Γ_p(x+1) = x·Γ_p(x)",c:false},{l:"C",t:"Γ_p(x+1) = Γ_p(x)",c:false},{l:"D",t:"Γ_p(x+1) = −Γ_p(x)",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Morita gamma function</strong> satisfies Γ_p(x+1) = h_p(x)·Γ_p(x) where h_p(x) = −x if x ∈ ℤ_p^× and h_p(x) = −1 if x ∈ pℤ_p. For x ∈ ℤ_p^×, Γ_p(x+1) = −x·Γ_p(x)."},{id:43248,text:"🧮 The Kubota-Leopoldt p-adic L-function interpolates:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"L(1−n, χω⁻ⁿ) for n ≥ 1",c:true},{l:"B",t:"L(s, χ) for all complex s",c:false},{l:"C",t:"Riemann zeta values ζ(n)",c:false},{l:"D",t:"Dedekind zeta values at s=0",c:false}],sol:"<strong>Kubota-Leopoldt L_p(s, χ)</strong> interpolates the values L(1−n, χω⁻ⁿ) for n ≥ 1, where ω is the Teichmüller character. This is the fundamental p-adic interpolation of Dirichlet L-functions."},{id:43249,text:"🧮 The Iwasawa main conjecture relates p-adic L-functions to:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"The characteristic ideals of class groups in ℤ_p-extensions",c:true},{l:"B",t:"The Riemann hypothesis",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The Birch and Swinnerton-Dyer conjecture",c:false},{l:"D",t:"Fermat's Last Theorem",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Iwasawa main conjecture</strong> (Mazur-Wiles, Wiles) equates the p-adic L-function to the characteristic ideal of the inverse limit of class groups along the cyclotomic ℤ_p-extension — a deep link between analytic and algebraic invariants."},{id:43250,text:"🔥 A p-adic representation V of Gal(̄ℚ_p/ℚ_p) is de Rham if:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"dim_{ℚ_p}(V ⊗ B_{dR})^{Gal} = dim_{ℚ_p} V",c:true},{l:"B",t:"It has finite image",c:false},{l:"C",t:"It is unramified",c:false},{l:"D",t:"dim V = 1",c:false}],sol:"<strong>De Rham representation</strong>: V is de Rham if the equality dim_{ℚ_p}(V ⊗_{ℚ_p} B_{dR})^{Gal} = dim_{ℚ_p} V holds, where B_{dR} is Fontaine's ring of p-adic periods."},{id:43251,text:"🔥 The Fargues-Fontaine curve is:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"A complete algebraic curve whose points correspond to untilts of perfectoid fields",c:true},{l:"B",t:"An elliptic curve over ℚ_p",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The projective line ℙ¹",c:false},{l:"D",t:"A modular curve",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Fargues-Fontaine curve</strong> is a complete algebraic curve over ℚ_p whose closed points parametrize equivalence classes of untilts of perfectoid fields. It is central to the geometric approach to p-adic Langlands."},{id:43252,text:"🔥 Scholze's tilting correspondence establishes:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"An equivalence of étale sites between a perfectoid field and its tilt",c:true},{l:"B",t:"An isomorphism of ℚ_p with 𝔽_p((t))",c:false},{l:"C",t:"A duality between Hodge and Tate cohomology",c:false},{l:"D",t:"A correspondence between ℚ_p and ℝ",c:false}],sol:"<strong>Scholze's tilting</strong>: for a perfectoid field K of characteristic 0, its tilt K^♭ is a perfectoid field of characteristic p, and there is an equivalence of étale sites between K and K^♭ — a powerful tool for transferring results from characteristic p to characteristic 0."}];
